What is MCP? 
MCP (Model Context Protocol) is an open standard that allows Al models (like ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, 
etc.) to securely connect with external tools, applications, databases, and APIs. 
One-line Definition 
MCP is like a USB-C port for Al. 
Just as USB-C lets different devices connect easily, MCP lets Al connect with different tools using one 
common standard. 
Why was MCP created? 
Without MCP: 
• Every Al tool needs a different integration. 
• Developers write custom code for each Al model. 
• Integration becomes difficult and expensive. 
